{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00439",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.1,
      "end_seconds": 5.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Um, uh, hello doctor, sorry, am I early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.31,
      "end_seconds": 9.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "You're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.22,
      "end_seconds": 19.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.13,
      "text": "Hmm, I'm here because of a routine check-up. Well, I've had mild headaches now and then too, for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.81,
      "end_seconds": 21.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.96,
      "end_seconds": 24.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.47,
      "end_seconds": 27.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Any occasional tiredness as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.75,
      "end_seconds": 30.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Oh, yes, for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.21,
      "end_seconds": 47.01,
      "duration_seconds": 13.8,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.0,
      "end_seconds": 51.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "I mean, okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.66,
      "end_seconds": 56.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Have you had any persistent cough, shortness of breath or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.83,
      "end_seconds": 62.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Oh, uh, no, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.31,
      "end_seconds": 65.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.24,
      "end_seconds": 68.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Oh, no, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.72,
      "end_seconds": 73.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.08,
      "end_seconds": 79.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Um, no, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.01,
      "end_seconds": 93.19,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.64,
      "end_seconds": 98.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.25,
      "end_seconds": 102.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.14,
      "end_seconds": 115.1,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "High cholesterol, for about ten years. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.63,
      "end_seconds": 117.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.98,
      "end_seconds": 124.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for two years. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.74,
      "end_seconds": 127.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Right. How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.72,
      "end_seconds": 132.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "I used to smoke but I quit five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.9,
      "end_seconds": 135.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.69,
      "end_seconds": 140.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.72,
      "end_seconds": 145.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.78,
      "end_seconds": 151.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.25,
      "end_seconds": 154.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "So, have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.76,
      "end_seconds": 160.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Yes, uh, I had a hernia repair, about five years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.31,
      "end_seconds": 164.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.82,
      "end_seconds": 169.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night. It's losartan, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.23,
      "end_seconds": 172.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.13,
      "end_seconds": 175.04,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "50 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.04,
      "end_seconds": 178.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.53,
      "end_seconds": 182.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Yeah, it's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 182.91,
      "end_seconds": 192.38,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Heart rate 74, pressure 124 over 72. Oxygen saturation is 99 percent, respiratory rate 18, temperature 36.7."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.85,
      "end_seconds": 197.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Thanks. Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.68,
      "end_seconds": 214.3,
      "duration_seconds": 15.62,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.12,
      "end_seconds": 219.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.75,
      "end_seconds": 220.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.13,
      "end_seconds": 224.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.56,
      "end_seconds": 245.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with no tenderness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.17,
      "end_seconds": 274.54,
      "duration_seconds": 26.37,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.98,
      "end_seconds": 279.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Thank you, uh, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.27,
      "end_seconds": 293.26,
      "duration_seconds": 12.99,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with generally well, nothing worrying today. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I'd also keep a tendency towards high cholesterol in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.04,
      "end_seconds": 311.49,
      "duration_seconds": 17.45,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.2,
      "end_seconds": 314.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "I, I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.42,
      "end_seconds": 323.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an HbA1c for health screening. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.09,
      "end_seconds": 327.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.54,
      "end_seconds": 343.77,
      "duration_seconds": 15.23,
      "text": "We should do a lipid profile for health screening. Keep up regular exercise, around a hundred and fifty minutes a week, and go easy on processed food. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.04,
      "end_seconds": 353.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "Mm. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.35,
      "end_seconds": 361.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Got it, um, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.03,
      "end_seconds": 370.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.74,
      "text": "Let's review you after the results are back. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.87,
      "end_seconds": 377.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "So, you know, I come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.98,
      "end_seconds": 382.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Okay, yes, exactly right. I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.5,
      "end_seconds": 387.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "That's all, you know, thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.9,
      "end_seconds": 390.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Alright, bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}